# M-inferred-cell step 1: a cell written and never read is told by the
# unused rule, `unused_binding`, and not by the never-re-bound rule, which
# asks only of a cell that IS read; so one cell gets one message whichever
# half of its life is missing.
function main()
    v: i64 @= 5           #~ unused_binding
    v @ 6
    print(1)
